'=============================================================================
' TrustLens — Data Flow Diagram set: Level 0, Level 1, Level 2
'
' Notation : DeMarco & Yourdon — oval = process, rectangle = external entity,
'            cylinder = data store (see note at the foot of this file)
' Balance  : L0's 18 flows all reappear at L1; 3.0's L1 flows all reappear at L2
' Derived from: PROGRAM-001 v1.1 · RESEARCH-001…005 · ADR-0003
' Status   : derived working figures, NOT the Phase 5 ARCH-001 artifact of record
'
' The web editor renders one diagram at a time — paste a single @startuml…@enduml
' block. The CLI and the VS Code extension render all three from this one file.
'=============================================================================


'#############################################################################
'#  LEVEL 0  —  CONTEXT DIAGRAM
'#  1 process · 9 external entities · 18 flows (9 in, 9 out) · no data stores
'#############################################################################
@startuml TrustLens_DFD_Level0

title <b>TrustLens  —  Level 0 Context Diagram</b>

skinparam backgroundColor #F8FAFC
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 11
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam dpi 150
skinparam nodesep 45
skinparam ranksep 130

<style>
element {
  Padding 8
  Margin  10
}
</style>

skinparam rectangle {
    BackgroundColor #1F3864
    FontColor       #FFFFFF
    BorderColor     #0D2137
    BorderThickness 2
}

skinparam usecase {
    BackgroundColor #BBDEFB
    BorderColor     #1565C0
    FontColor       #0D2137
    BorderThickness 2
}

skinparam arrow {
    Color       #444444
    FontColor   #222222
    FontSize    9
}

left to right direction

rectangle "Reporting User\n(P1 Priya / P2 Ramesh)"       as RU
rectangle "Analyst\n(P3 Anjali)"                          as AN
rectangle "Administrator\n(P6)"                           as AD
rectangle "Report Recipient\n(authority / bank / portal)" as RR
rectangle "Official Guidance Bodies\n(I4C / CERT-In / RBI /\nNPCI / SEBI / DoT)" as GB
rectangle "Knowledge Editor\n(P4 Vikram)"                 as KE
rectangle "Knowledge Approver\n(P5 Meera)"                as KA
rectangle "Threat-Intel Providers\n(post-MVP)"            as TI
rectangle "AI Assist Provider\n(post-MVP)"                as AI

usecase "**0.0**\n**TrustLens**\nScam Detection,\nEvidence &\nReporting System" as SYS

RU -right-> SYS : F1  Submitted artifacts\n(SMS, chat, email, URL, screenshot)
RU -right-> SYS : F2  Correction,\nre-evaluate request
SYS  -left-> RU : F3  Verdict, risk + confidence,\nevidence trace, citations
SYS  -left-> RU : F4  Report bundle\n+ integrity hashes

SYS  -left-> AN : F5  Queued uncertain case\n+ score decomposition
AN -right-> SYS : F6  Adjudication\n+ rationale

AD -right-> SYS : F7  Configuration,\nretention policy
SYS  -left-> AD : F8  Health, audit events,\nmetrics

SYS  -left-> RR : F9  Access-controlled export\n(never auto-submitted)

GB   -left-> SYS : F10  Published advisories\n(one way, graded before use)

KE   -left-> SYS : F11  Draft rule\n+ graded sources
SYS -right-> KE  : F12  Schema + lint verdict

SYS -right-> KA  : F13  Diff, impact analysis,\nregression replay
KA   -left-> SYS : F14  Publish / reject\ndecision

SYS -right-> TI  : F15  Reputation lookup
TI   -left-> SYS : F16  Provider verdict

SYS -right-> AI  : F17  Isolated content prompt
AI   -left-> SYS : F18  Schema-checked draft\n(human approval required)

legend bottom left
  9 flows in · 9 flows out · no data stores at level 0
  The rule set decides — AI is never the decision authority
endlegend

@enduml


'#############################################################################
'#  LEVEL 1  —  8 processes (ceiling is 9) · 6 data stores · 9 terminators
'#  Every one of the 18 level-0 flows reappears here, by ID.
'#############################################################################
@startuml TrustLens_DFD_Level1

title <b>TrustLens  —  Level 1 DFD</b>

skinparam backgroundColor #F8FAFC
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 10
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam dpi 150
skinparam nodesep 40
skinparam ranksep 90

<style>
element {
  Padding 6
  Margin  8
}
</style>

skinparam rectangle {
    BackgroundColor #1F3864
    FontColor       #FFFFFF
    BorderColor     #0D2137
    BorderThickness 2
}

skinparam usecase {
    BackgroundColor #BBDEFB
    BorderColor     #1565C0
    FontColor       #0D2137
    BorderThickness 2
}

skinparam database {
    BackgroundColor #FFF8E1
    BorderColor     #E65100
    FontColor       #4E342E
    BorderThickness 2
}

skinparam arrow {
    Color       #444444
    FontColor   #222222
    FontSize    9
}

rectangle "Reporting User"          as RU
rectangle "Analyst"                 as AN
rectangle "Administrator"           as AD
rectangle "Report Recipient"        as RR
rectangle "Guidance Bodies"         as GB
rectangle "Knowledge Editor"        as KE
rectangle "Knowledge Approver"      as KA
rectangle "Threat-Intel Providers"  as TI
rectangle "AI Assist Provider"      as AI

usecase "**1.0**\nIngest &\nPreserve Evidence"      as P1
usecase "**2.0**\nNormalise &\nExtract"             as P2
usecase "**3.0**\nEvaluate Rules\n& Score"          as P3
usecase "**4.0**\nCompose\nExplanation"             as P4
usecase "**5.0**\nRoute &\nAdjudicate"              as P5
usecase "**6.0**\nAssemble\nReport Bundle"          as P6
usecase "**7.0**\nGovern\nKnowledge Base"           as P7
usecase "**8.0**\nAdminister,\nAudit & Observe"     as P8

database "D1  Evidence\nStore"        as D1
database "D2  Case\nStore"            as D2
database "D3  Rule-Set\nStore"        as D3
database "D4  Source\nRegister"       as D4
database "D5  Analysis\nRecord"       as D5
database "D6  Audit\nLog"             as D6

' --- ingest -----------------------------------------------------------------
RU -down-> P1 : F1  Submitted artifacts
P1 --> D1 : Artifact + SHA-256 hash,\nchain of custody
D1 --> P2 : Preserved artifact

' --- normalise and extract --------------------------------------------------
RU -down-> P2 : F2  Corrections,\nre-evaluate
P2 -right-> AI : F17  Isolated content prompt
P2 --> P3 : Entities, indicators,\nnegative indicators

' --- evaluate ---------------------------------------------------------------
D3 --> P3 : Published rule set\n(version pinned)
P3 -right-> TI : F15  Reputation lookup
TI -left-> P3 : F16  Provider verdict
P3 --> D5 : Pinned analysis record\n(for exact replay)
P3 --> P4 : Matched / unmatched rules,\nrisk + confidence
P3 --> P5 : Uncertain case\n(past threshold)

' --- explain ----------------------------------------------------------------
D4 --> P4 : Graded source citations
P4 -up-> RU : F3  Verdict + evidence trace

' --- adjudicate -------------------------------------------------------------
P5 -up-> AN : F5  Queued case\n+ decomposition
AN -down-> P5 : F6  Adjudication\n+ rationale
P5 --> D2 : Case, findings,\nadjudication
P5 --> D6 : Adjudication audit event

' --- report -----------------------------------------------------------------
D2 --> P6 : Case + findings
D1 --> P6 : Evidence + hashes
D5 --> P6 : Pinned analysis\n(reproducible)
P6 -up-> RU : F4  Report bundle
P6 --> RR : F9  Access-controlled export

' --- knowledge governance ---------------------------------------------------
GB --> P7 : F10  Published advisories
P7 --> D4 : Graded source record
KE --> P7 : F11  Draft rule + sources
P7 --> KE : F12  Schema + lint verdict
P7 --> KA : F13  Diff, impact, replay
KA --> P7 : F14  Publish / reject
AI --> P7 : F18  Schema-checked draft
P7 --> D3 : Publish rule-set version
P7 --> D6 : Knowledge action audit

' --- administration ---------------------------------------------------------
AD --> P8 : F7  Config, retention policy
P8 --> AD : F8  Health, audit, metrics
D6 --> P8 : Audit events

@enduml


'#############################################################################
'#  LEVEL 2  —  process 3.0 exploded into 3.1 … 3.5
'#  Conserves every flow 3.0 owns at level 1 (balancing).
'#############################################################################
@startuml TrustLens_DFD_Level2_EvaluateRulesAndScore

title <b>TrustLens  —  Level 2 DFD  |  Process 3.0: Evaluate Rules & Score</b>

skinparam backgroundColor #F8FAFC
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 10
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam dpi 150
skinparam nodesep 45
skinparam ranksep 110

<style>
element {
  Padding 6
  Margin  8
}
</style>

skinparam rectangle {
    BackgroundColor #1F3864
    FontColor       #FFFFFF
    BorderColor     #0D2137
    BorderThickness 2
}

skinparam usecase {
    BackgroundColor #BBDEFB
    BorderColor     #1565C0
    FontColor       #0D2137
    BorderThickness 2
}

skinparam database {
    BackgroundColor #FFF8E1
    BorderColor     #E65100
    FontColor       #4E342E
    BorderThickness 2
}

skinparam arrow {
    Color       #444444
    FontColor   #222222
    FontSize    9
}

left to right direction

rectangle "Threat-Intel Providers"          as TI
rectangle "[2.0]\nNormalise &\nExtract"      as P2REF
rectangle "[4.0]\nCompose\nExplanation"      as P4REF
rectangle "[5.0]\nRoute &\nAdjudicate"       as P5REF

usecase "**3.1**\nLoad & Pin\nRule Set"                  as P31
usecase "**3.2**\nMatch\nComposite Rules"                as P32
usecase "**3.3**\nApply Suppressors\n& Resolve Conflicts" as P33
usecase "**3.4**\nScore Risk &\nConfidence\nSeparately"   as P34
usecase "**3.5**\nDecide Outcome\n& Route"                as P35

database "D3  Rule-Set\nStore"    as D3
database "D5  Analysis\nRecord"   as D5

D3 -down-> P31 : Published rules, indicators,\ntaxonomy version
D5   -up-> P31 : Replay request:\npinned rule-set version
P31 -right-> P32 : Pinned rule set\n(version id fixed)

P2REF -right-> P32 : Entities, indicators,\nnegative indicators

P32 -right-> TI : F15  Reputation lookup
TI   -left-> P32 : F16  Provider verdict\n(labelled non-authoritative)

P32 -right-> P33 : Candidate rule matches\n(composite triggers met)
P33 -right-> P34 : Surviving matches\n+ suppressed set
P34 -right-> P35 : Risk, confidence, severity,\nevidence quality (4 separate values)

P35 -down-> D5 : Pinned analysis record\n(inputs, version, scores)
P35   -up-> P4REF : Findings + full\nscore decomposition
P35 -down-> P5REF : Uncertain case /\nINSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE

legend bottom left
  5 sub-processes (ceiling is 9)
  Suppressors run before scoring, so negative evidence can never be out-voted
endlegend

@enduml

'=============================================================================
' NOTE ON THE DATA-STORE SYMBOL
' Slide 6 / 9 of the deck define a data store as an OPEN RECTANGLE, not a
' cylinder. PlantUML has no open-rectangle shape, so this file uses `database`
' (the cylinder), which is the common PlantUML substitute. If your evaluator
' wants the deck's symbol exactly, change each `database "D1 …" as D1` line to
'     rectangle "D1  |  Evidence Store" as D1
' and add a store-specific skinparam block.
'=============================================================================
